ggml-metal: memory ranges that only touch do not overlap

ggml_mem_ranges_check treats ranges as half-open, [p0, p1) (its debug
message prints them so, and p1 = data + alloc size), but tested
mr.p1 >= cmp.p0: a source that ends exactly where an earlier destination
begins counted as overlapping, and the encoder put a barrier between two
independent kernels. ggml-hexagon's copy of the same check uses '>'.
Seen in DynaLM: ggml_gallocr placed a Q projection's output directly after
the normed input that the K projection reads, so K waited for Q.

--- a/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp	2026-10-20 01:10:51
+++ b/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp	2026-10-20 01:10:51
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@
             continue;
         }
 
-        if (mr.p0 < cmp.p1 && mr.p1 >= cmp.p0) {
+        if (mr.p0 < cmp.p1 && mr.p1 > cmp.p0) {
             if (mrs->debug > 2) {
                 GGML_LOG_DEBUG("%s: the %s range buf=%lld, [%lld, %lld) overlaps with a previous %s range buf=%lld, [%lld, %lld)\n",
                         __func__,
